{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"sec-appendix-d-finite-norms-and-coefficient-estimates","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:56af3c7e2758851c18ce1c7cfe419208686d0442345d09615ed71c6050bb11ef/papers/short.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/short?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196","passage_ref":"sha256:a1593370c38e12db1c19bd7e6926ae58ff48cf2267100066f3070a6a2aaeb22c/papers/short.md/sha256:56af3c7e2758851c18ce1c7cfe419208686d0442345d09615ed71c6050bb11ef/papers/short.json/passages/sec-appendix-d-finite-norms-and-coefficient-estimates","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&paper=short&passage=sec-appendix-d-finite-norms-and-coefficient-estimates","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&paper=short&passage=sec-appendix-d-finite-norms-and-coefficient-estimates","span":{"end_byte":215168,"end_line":1618,"start_byte":207220,"start_line":1551},"stage":"short"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&view=arguments&node=euler.lemma-d.3&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&node=euler.lemma-d.3&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&node=euler.lemma-d.3&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&view=arguments&node=euler.lemma-d.3&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&ref=sha256%3Ab6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b%2Fnodes%2Feuler.lemma-d.3","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"A result as the authors number it. Its links to the Lean were made with AI for Proof Reader and have not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.euler.lemma-d.3"],"evidence_ids":["link.euler.lemma-d.3"],"id":"euler.lemma-d.3","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma D.3","locator":"Lemma D.3, Section D","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma D.3.** Consider a linear equation of the form $$\\mathcal Lv=\\mathcal L_0v+\\sum_\\nu T_\\nu(c_\\nu v)=F$$ with finitely many phase-independent coefficients $c_\\nu(t,a)$. Assume that $\\mathcal L_0$ and the linear operators $T_\\nu$ commute with label and phase derivatives. The equation may hold modulo a fixed subspace, such as gradients. Assume that differentiation preserves this subspace and the linear constraints on $v$, and commutes with the maps giving any prescribed data. Write $f$ for the forcing $F$ together with these data, with the sum of their norms. Suppose that for every admissible source one has the estimate $$\\|v\\|_{[0],\\gamma}\\le C_{\\rm low}\\|f\\|_{[0],\\gamma}.$$ Let $b_\\nu$ be the operator norm of $T_\\nu$ from $\\|\\cdot\\|_{[0],\\gamma}$ to the forcing norm. If $$\\begin{equation}\n C_{\\rm low}\\sum_\\nu b_\\nu\\ell_*^m|c_\\nu|_m\\le C_m\\qquad(m\\ge1), \\tag{D.7}\n\\end{equation}$$ then every smooth solution satisfies, for $n\\ge0$, $$\\|v\\|_{[n],\\gamma}\\le C_n C_{\\rm low}\\|f\\|_{[n],\\gamma}.$$ Here $C_n$ depends only on $n$ and the bounds $C_m$ in (D.7) for $m\\le n$. For phase-independent fields with $\\gamma\\equiv1$, the same assertion holds using $\\|\\cdot\\|_{[n],1/2}$ and $|c_\\nu|_{m,1/2}$ throughout, with $b_\\nu$ taken in the corresponding zero-order norms.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-d.3","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-5.3","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc